Subject: [PATCH] text: UTF-8 font rendering with a 224-cell Latin-1 atlas

Font::Glyph() now takes a char32_t and maps U+0020..U+00FF onto the atlas;
DrawAliased() and WidthRawString() decode UTF-8 instead of iterating bytes.
Requires images/font/ubuntu{14,18}r_it.png generated by tools/font_extend.py
(224 cells) copied over the original atlas, or GLYPHS must be reverted.

--- a/source/text/Font.h
+++ b/source/text/Font.h
@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@
 
 
 private:
-	static int Glyph(char c, bool isAfterSpace) noexcept;
+	static int Glyph(char32_t c, bool isAfterSpace) noexcept;
